meta {
  name: Bulk edit
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bills/bulk/edit
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{billId}}"],
    "fields": {
      "dueDate": "2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z",
      "invoiceDate": "2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "description": "Updated in bulk"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Admin only. Applies the same field updates to every non-terminal
  bill in `ids`. Allowed fields: `dueDate`, `invoiceDate`,
  `description`. At least one must be present; an empty `fields`
  object is rejected with 400. Terminal bills
  (PAID/REJECTED/ARCHIVED) fail per item with BILL_NOT_EDITABLE.

  `amount` is intentionally NOT bulk-editable. The spec lists it, but
  bulk-setting the same monetary value across N distinct invoices is
  almost never the correct operation; AP teams that need batch
  amount changes should reach for a CSV import flow (out of scope).
  `paymentMethod` is also excluded — it lives on the Payment row,
  not the Bill, once the bill is approved.

  Response shape: `{ results: [{ id, ok, data? | error? }], summary }`.
  Always HTTP 200; empty / duplicate `ids` -> 400 BULK_INVALID_IDS.
  See `bills/bulk/approve.bru` for the full envelope.
}
